[' To create an efficient HTTP request processor in C#, I'll provide you with a basic implementation using `SemaphoreSlim` for concurrency control and `TaskCompletionSource` for managing tasks. This solution is designed to handle large volumes of concurrent requests, error handling, scalability, and integration challenges.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Concurrent;
using System.Linq;
using System.Net.Http;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public class HttpRequestProcessor
{
    private readonly SemaphoreSlim _semaphore;
    private readonly ConcurrentDictionary<string, TaskCompletionSource<HttpResponseMessage>> _requests;
    private readonly HttpClient _httpClient;
    private readonly TimeSpan _timeout;
    private readonly int _maxDegreeOfParallelism;

    public HttpRequestProcessor(HttpClient httpClient, TimeSpan timeout, int maxDegreeOfParallelism)
    {
        _httpClient = httpClient;
        _timeout = timeout;
        _maxDegreeOfParallelism = maxDegreeOfParallelism;
        _semaphore = new SemaphoreSlim(maxDegreeOfParallelism);
        _requests = new ConcurrentDictionary<string, TaskCompletionSource<HttpResponseMessage>>();
    }

    public async Task ProcessRequestsAsync(IEnumerable<string> urls)
    {
        var tasks = urls.Select(url =>
        {
            var tcs = new TaskCompletionSource<HttpResponseMessage>();
            _requests[url] = tcs;

            return _semaphore.WaitAsync().ContinueWith(_ =>
            {
                if (!_semaphore.CurrentCount > 0) return;

                _semaphore.Release();

                Task.Run(async () =>
                {
                    try
                    {
                        var response = await _httpClient.GetAsync(url, HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead);
                        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode)
                        {
                            tcs.SetException(new Exception($"Request to '{url}' failed with status code: {response.StatusCode}"));
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            tcs.SetResult(response);
                        }
                    }
                    catch (Exception ex)
                    {
                        tcs.SetException(ex);
                    }
                });
            });
        });

        await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
    }

    public void CancelRequest(string url) => _requests[url].TrySetCanceled();
}
```

This implementation creates a `HttpRequestProcessor` class that accepts an `HttpClient`, timeout value, and maximum degree of parallelism. The `ProcessRequestsAsync` method processes the given URLs concurrently with the specified degree of parallelism. It uses a `SemaphoreSlim` to limit the number of concurrent requests and a `TaskCompletionSource` to manage each request's response.

The solution also includes error handling, cancellation support, and integration challenges such as retry logic with exponential backoff can be added by modifying the inner Task that handles the actual HTTP request.']

