To handle large XML files, you can modify the code to process them in manageable chunks instead of loading the entire file into memory at once. This can be achieved by reading the XML file line by line and adding each line to the XML document as an element before processing the XPath query.

The cache size is set to 100 documents, but you can adjust this value based on your specific requirements. Keep in mind that a larger cache size will improve performance for repeated queries but may consume more memory. Conversely, a smaller cache size will reduce memory usage but may impact performance for frequent queries.

