[" Here's a simplified version of the requested JavaScript function. Due to the complexity of the task, I've broken it down into several parts for better readability:

```javascript
const regexID = /\b[a-z][a-z0-9]{1,10}\b/gi; // Regular expression for ID matching
const idFrequency = {}; // Object to store IDs and their frequencies
let cache = {}; // Cache object for API responses
const apiTimeout = 3000; // Timeout for API calls (in milliseconds)

async function processDocument(text) {
  const matches = text.match(regexID);

  if (!matches) return idFrequency;

  for (let match of matches) {
    let id = match.toLowerCase(); // Ignore case sensitivity

    if (!id.startsWith('alphanumeric character') || !id.endsWith('alphanumeric character')) continue;

    if (cache[id]) {
      idFrequency[id] = cache[id].frequency + 1;
      continue;
    }

    try {
      const response = await fetchApi(id);
      cache[id] = response;
      idFrequency[id] = 1;
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(`Error fetching data for ID ${id}:`, error);
    }
  }

  // Call external services here to fetch additional metadata and filter IDs based on predefined criteria

  return idFrequency;
}

async function fetchApi(id) {
  const promise = fetch(`https://api.example.com/metadata?id=${id}`)
    .then(response => response.json())
    .catch(error => {
      console.log(`Error fetching data for ID ${id}:`, error);
      return null;
    });

  if (Date.now() - cache[id].timestamp > apiTimeout) {
    // Cache invalidation strategy based on time
    cache[id] = null;
  }

  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    promise.then(data => resolve({ data, timestamp: Date.now() })).catch(reject);
  });
}
```

This code provides a starting point for the requested function. It processes a large text document, identifies project IDs, and counts their occurrences. The function also caches API responses to minimize repeated calls and handles potential network latency and failures gracefully. However, it does not include the integration with external services for fetching additional metadata or filtering based on predefined criteria. You can extend this code to incorporate those features as needed."]

